{"task_id": "HumanEval/20", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\ndef find_closest_elements(numbers: List[float]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Identifies and returns the two closest numbers from the input list, ordered from smallest to largest.\"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list must contain at least two numbers.\")\n\n    # Sort the list to efficiently find the closest elements.\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    closest_pair: Tuple[float, float] = (0.0, 0.0)\n\n    # Iterate through adjacent elements to find the minimum difference.\n    for i in range(len(sorted_numbers) - 1):\n        diff = sorted_numbers[i+1] - sorted_numbers[i]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n            closest_pair = (sorted_numbers[i], sorted_numbers[i+1])\n    \n    return closest_pair"}
