{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "def decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes an encoded string and returns the original, decoded string.\n    Reverses the cyclic shift applied to groups of three characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_parts = []\n    # Split string into groups of three characters.\n    for i in range(0, len(s), 3):\n        group = s[i:i+3]\n        if len(group) == 3:\n            # Apply inverse cyclic shift: original was group[2] + group[0] + group[1]\n            decoded_parts.append(group[2] + group[0] + group[1])\n        else:\n            # Groups of fewer than three characters are left unchanged.\n            decoded_parts.append(group)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_parts)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "def sort_even(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'l' must be a list.\")\n\n    if not l:  # Handle empty list\n        return []\n\n    # Extract elements at even indices and sort them.\n    even_indexed_elements = [l[i] for i in range(0, len(l), 2)]\n    even_indexed_elements.sort()\n\n    # Construct the new list, placing sorted even-indexed elements and original odd-indexed elements.\n    result_list = [None] * len(l)\n    sorted_even_counter = 0\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            result_list[i] = even_indexed_elements[sorted_even_counter]\n            sorted_even_counter += 1\n        else:\n            result_list[i] = l[i]\n\n    return result_list"}
