{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\n    It indicates that input values do not meet the function's requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\ndef modp(n: int, p: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using modular exponentiation.\n    Handles large n efficiently and validates inputs for correctness.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if p <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'p' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 % p\n\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1: # If n is odd, multiply current result with base\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p # Square the base and halve n for next iteration\n        n //= 2\n    \n    return result"}
