{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circularly shifts digits of an integer to the right or reverses them.\n    Returns the result as a string, handling shift amount exceeding digit count.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_digits = str(x)\n    num_digits = len(str_digits)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        # If shift is strictly greater than the number of digits, reverse.\n        return str_digits[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Perform circular right shift by the effective amount.\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        return str_digits[-effective_shift:] + str_digits[:-effective_shift]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "def vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Counts vowels ('a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u') in a word. 'y' is counted only if it's the last character.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n\n    if not s_lower:\n        return 0\n\n    standard_vowels = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(s_lower):\n        if char in standard_vowels:\n            count += 1\n        elif char == 'y' and i == len(s_lower) - 1:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
