{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "import math\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    return xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[1] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs are coefficients of a polynomial.\n    find_zero find x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    find_zero returns only only zero point, even if there are many.\n    Moreover, find_zero only takes list xs having even number of coefficients\n    and largest non zero coefficient as it guarantees\n    a solution.\n    >>> round(find_zero([1, 2]), 2) # f(x) = 1 + 2x\n    -0.5\n    >>> round(find_zero([-6, 11, -6, 1]), 2) # (x - 1) * (x - 2) * (x - 3) = -6 + 11x - 6x^2 + x^3\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    # Constants for the solver.\n    TOLERANCE: float = 1e-6\n    MAX_ITERATIONS: int = 1000\n    INITIAL_SEARCH_BOUND: float = 1.0\n    MAX_SEARCH_BOUND: float = 1e10\n    EPSILON_ZERO_CHECK: float = 1e-9\n\n    if not xs or len(xs) % 2 != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Coefficients list 'xs' must not be empty and must have an even number of elements.\")\n\n    # Handle the edge case where 0 is a root directly.\n    if abs(poly(xs, 0.0)) < EPSILON_ZERO_CHECK:\n        return 0.0\n\n    low = -INITIAL_SEARCH_BOUND\n    high = INITIAL_SEARCH_BOUND\n\n    # Find an initial interval [low, high] where poly(low) and poly(high) have opposite signs.\n    p_low = poly(xs, low)\n    p_high = poly(xs, high)\n\n    search_iterations = 0\n    while p_low * p_high >= 0:\n        if abs(low) > MAX_SEARCH_BOUND or abs(high) > MAX_SEARCH_BOUND:\n            # According to the problem statement, a solution is guaranteed.\n            # If this is hit, it implies an extreme scenario or problem with bounds.\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not find an initial interval within bounds [-{MAX_SEARCH_BOUND}, {MAX_SEARCH_BOUND}]\")\n\n        low *= 2.0\n        high *= 2.0\n        p_low = poly(xs, low)\n        p_high = poly(xs, high)\n        search_iterations += 1\n        if search_iterations > MAX_ITERATIONS * 2:\n             raise RuntimeError(\"Exceeded search iterations for initial interval expansion.\")\n\n\n    # Apply the bisection method within the established interval.\n    iterations = 0\n    while (high - low) > TOLERANCE and iterations < MAX_ITERATIONS:\n        mid = (low + high) / 2.0\n        p_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n        if abs(p_mid) < EPSILON_ZERO_CHECK:\n            return mid\n\n        if p_low * p_mid < 0:\n            high = mid\n            # Update p_high to avoid re-evaluating poly(xs, high).\n            p_high = p_mid\n        else:\n            low = mid\n            # Update p_low to avoid re-evaluating poly(xs, low).\n            p_low = p_mid\n        iterations += 1\n\n    # Return the midpoint of the final interval as the zero point.\n    return (low + high) / 2.0"}
