{"task_id": "HumanEval/108", "solution": "def count_nums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts numbers in an array where the sum of their digits is greater than zero.\n    The first digit of a negative number is treated as negative for sum calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_digit_sum_for_num(num):\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the sum of signed digits for an integer.\n        For negative numbers, the first digit is negative.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        is_negative = num < 0\n        abs_num_str = str(abs(num))\n        \n        total_sum = 0\n        for i, digit_char in enumerate(abs_num_str):\n            digit = int(digit_char)\n            if i == 0 and is_negative:\n                total_sum += -digit\n            else:\n                total_sum += digit\n        return total_sum\n\n    count = 0\n    for num in arr:\n        if _calculate_digit_sum_for_num(num) > 0:\n            count += 1\n            \n    return count"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/108", "solution": "def count_nums(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts numbers in an array whose sum of digits is greater than zero.\n    Handles negative numbers by treating the first digit after the minus sign as negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n\n    def _calculate_digit_sum(num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of digits for a number according to the specified rules.\"\"\"\n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        s_num = str(num)\n        total_sum = 0\n        \n        if num < 0:\n            # The first digit after the minus sign is treated as negative.\n            total_sum += int(s_num[1]) * -1\n            # Subsequent digits are treated as positive.\n            for digit_char in s_num[2:]:\n                total_sum += int(digit_char)\n        else:\n            # All digits are treated as positive for positive numbers.\n            for digit_char in s_num:\n                total_sum += int(digit_char)\n                \n        return total_sum\n\n    for num in arr:\n        sum_of_digits = _calculate_digit_sum(num)\n        if sum_of_digits > 0:\n            count += 1\n            \n    return count"}
