{"task_id": "HumanEval/148", "solution": "PLANET_ORDER = [\n    \"Mercury\", \"Venus\", \"Earth\", \"Mars\", \"Jupiter\",\n    \"Saturn\", \"Uranus\", \"Neptune\"\n]\ndef bf(planet1, planet2):\n    '''\n    Finds planets orbiting between two specified planets, sorted by proximity to the Sun.\n    Returns an empty tuple if inputs are invalid or no planets are found between them.\n    '''\n    if planet1 not in PLANET_ORDER or planet2 not in PLANET_ORDER:\n        return ()\n\n    idx1 = PLANET_ORDER.index(planet1)\n    idx2 = PLANET_ORDER.index(planet2)\n\n    # If the planets are the same, or adjacent, there are no planets in between.\n    if abs(idx1 - idx2) <= 1:\n        return ()\n\n    start_idx = min(idx1, idx2)\n    end_idx = max(idx1, idx2)\n\n    # Slice the list to get planets between the two indices.\n    intermediate_planets = PLANET_ORDER[start_idx + 1:end_idx]\n\n    return tuple(intermediate_planets)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "import math\ndef x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns x if n is a prime number, and y otherwise.\n    A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 with no divisors other than 1 and itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Determine if n is a prime number, following FR1 and BR1.\n    is_prime_number = True\n    if n < 2:  # Numbers less than 2 are not prime (edge case handling).\n        is_prime_number = False\n    else:\n        # Check for divisibility from 2 up to the square root of n for efficiency (NFR1).\n        for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                is_prime_number = False\n                break\n    \n    # Return x or y based on primality (FR2, FR3).\n    if is_prime_number:\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "def double_the_difference(lst):\n    # Given a list of numbers, return the sum of squares of the numbers\n    # that are positive, odd integers.\n    total_sum = 0\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    for num in lst:\n        # Check if the number is an integer, positive, and odd.\n        if isinstance(num, int) and num > 0 and num % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += num * num\n    return total_sum"}
