{"task_id": "HumanEval/131", "solution": "def digits(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the product of all odd digits in a positive integer n.\n    Returns 0 if no odd digits are found.\"\"\"\n    \n    product = 1\n    has_odd_digit = False\n    \n    # Iterate through each digit by converting the integer to a string.\n    for char_digit in str(n):\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        # Multiply only if the digit is odd.\n        if digit % 2 != 0:\n            product *= digit\n            has_odd_digit = True\n            \n    # Return 0 if no odd digits were present, otherwise return the computed product.\n    if not has_odd_digit:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        return product"}
